# Line-ending normalization, added 2026-08-08.
#
# WHY: without this, a two-line change produced a WHOLE-FILE diff. audit-spec-contradictions.ps1 showed 709
# changed lines for a 2-line edit; `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` reduced it to 9. core.autocrlf is true, but
# with no .gitattributes the repo had a mixed CR state, so any tool writing CRLF into an LF-stored file
# rewrote every line as far as git was concerned. A diff nobody can read is a review nobody performs, and
# this estate reviews by reading diffs.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF IN THE REPOSITORY while letting core.autocrlf decide the working copy, so
# nothing about how these files appear on Brad's Windows box changes.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT RENORMALIZED IN BULK. `git add --renormalize .` would fix the whole history-facing state
# in one commit touching hundreds of files - and would collide with the daily pipeline bot, which commits and
# rebases onto main on its own schedule. Files normalize as they are touched instead. The big diff never
# needs to happen; it just stops getting worse.
* text=auto

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.wav  binary
*.zip  binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
